// SPEC qa.md appendix section 1: RESERVED type words are `U<N>`/`S<N>`/Unsigned/Signed/Bool/String/Clock/Reset;
// section 7: BANNED words are the LOWERCASE `u8`, `s20`, `i32` (any u/s/i + digits) ... . `I<N>` is removed
// (not reserved, not banned). Rule probed: an uppercase `I8` is an ordinary name.
const I8 = 3
cassert(I8 == 3)
